# Boss_CatHead_EyeFxAt: no corpus run calls it (ruling 5, 2). Its callers: the bra.s of the eye spark
# natives and the fall-through of Boss_CatHead_EyeShotAt, which hand it d0 = the eye's x offset and
# a0 = the a4 script. The case runs at Boss_CatHead_DriverSettle's first corpus call ($03BAB4), a
# native the same VM enters with the object's registers, with what Boss_CatHead_EyeSparkLeft passes
# on: d0 = -$1E, a0 = Scr4_03B7F2, a2 = the operand of its Op2_CallNativeRel at $03C44C. Without a0
# set, Fx_RunScript ran the code bytes at $03BAB4 as a script, and the two runs' last RTS differed
# (the generated SwayPoint's vs the C call's own; 2026-10-30). raw-stubs 2026-10-30.
at $03BAB4

case as_spark_left
reg d0 = $0000FFE2
reg a0 = $0003B7F2
reg a2 = $0003C450
